                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "Bobo is a solo project by a new dev, so I expected some rough edges which I'm totally fine with. \n\nI'm a huge 3D platformer fan. I have played all of the big ones on all the consoles and a ton of the indies like Kiwi 64, Cavern of Dreams, Lunistice, Yellow Taxi Goes Vroom,  Misc A Tiny Tale, Cirno!, POI, etc.  Based on my first couple of hours with the game, I have to say Bobo is one of the weaker games in the genre. \n\nThe demo level is quite good. The other levels I played were far more flat and generic feeling with little variety to separate them. Nearly every enemy is the same mechanically with different art. They just run at you and punch and I was randomly unable to jump on some of them because of buggy collider issues. \n\nThe overall presentation is pretty good. It has a generally nice mood and atmosphere that compliments the theme. Some of the SFX are too loud and ignore the audio slider. \n\nThe collectathon aspect is confusing with 3 identical moon crystals being in each level, but one of them is the \"main one\" which ends the level if you pick it up. So if you are trying to complete a level, you have to guess which ones are not the main, or you will have to replay the level. There are a LOT of gems to collect which I love, but some of them are hidden and invisible making it very difficult to collect them all. \n\nI would have continued playing to see if it gets better, but the map clearly being undisclosed AI art is an automatic refund for me.",
